name,layers,table,aoi_deg,reference
MgF2,mgf2:qw@550,,,"Single-layer AR coating, quarter-wave MgF2 at 550nm (classic AR design, e.g. Macleod 'Thin-Film Optical Filters')"
MgF2_133,mgf2:100.0,,,"MgF2 at a fixed literal thickness of 100nm (illustrates the <thickness_nm> spec form, close to quarter-wave near 545nm)"
BBAR_MgF2_SiO2,sio2_film:25;mgf2:qw@550,,,"Illustrative two-layer broadband-AR-style stack (SiO2 spacer + quarter-wave MgF2 outer layer); illustrative values, not a validated broadband design"
Al_mirror_bare,aluminum:80.0,,,"Bare (unprotected) aluminum mirror coating, typical physical-vapor-deposited thickness; illustrative"
Au_mirror_bare,gold:100.0,,,"Bare gold mirror coating, typical thickness for IR mirrors; illustrative"
hot_mirror_45,,hot_mirror_45.mietab,45,"modeled on Edmund Optics TECHSPEC 45deg AOI Hot Mirror (e.g. #19177/#5424 series): >90% (some models >85%) average transmission of visible, >95% average reflection of IR at 45deg AOI; vendor page gives band-average specs only (curve graph not machine-fetchable), so the s/p-split sigmoid edge shape here (edge blue-shifted for s-pol, red-shifted for p-pol, typical of oblique-incidence dielectric edge filters) is an engineering approximation anchored to those average numbers -- www.edmundoptics.com/f/hot-mirrors/11665/"
cold_mirror_45,,cold_mirror_45.mietab,45,"modeled on Edmund Optics TECHSPEC 45deg AOI Cold Mirror (e.g. #19159/#19162 series): >95% average reflection of visible, >90% average transmission of IR at 45deg AOI; same approximation method as hot_mirror_45 (band-average vendor spec, not a curve digitization) -- www.edmundoptics.com/c/hot-cold-mirrors/989/"
pbs_visible_45,,pbs_visible_45.mietab,45,"modeled on Thorlabs PBS251 broadband polarizing beamsplitter cube (N-SF1 glass, 420-680nm, Tp:Ts > 1000:1 on the transmitted arm per product page; reflected-arm extinction is much lower, ~20:1-100:1 typical of PBS cubes); Tp/Ts/Rs/Rp wavelength shape is an engineering approximation (best extinction mid-band, degrading toward the 420/680nm edges) anchored to the >1000:1 spec, not a digitized curve -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=PBS251"
dichroic_567lp_45,,dichroic_567lp_45.mietab,45,"modeled on Thorlabs DMLP567 longpass dichroic mirror/beamsplitter (fused silica, ion-beam-sputtered hard coating; cut-on(50%)=567nm, Ravg>90% over 380-550nm, Tavg>90% over 584-700nm per product page); the 550-584nm transition and s/p split (~14nm, typical of 45deg dielectric edge filters) plus the >700nm extension to 1100nm are engineering approximations, not a digitization of Thorlabs' 200-2600nm raw data file -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=DMLP567"
bs_5050_vis_45,,bs_5050_vis_45.mietab,45,"modeled on Thorlabs BS013 non-polarizing 50:50 beamsplitter cube (N-BK7, 400-700nm, broadband AR-coated external faces, R<0.5% average per-surface); internal beamsplitter coating modeled as Rs~Rp~0.48-0.52 with ~2% total absorption (Rs+Ts=Rp+Tp=0.98), small residual s/p ripple typical of non-polarizing cube coatings -- exact Rs/Rp/Ts/Tp vendor curve not published/machine-fetchable, so this is an engineering approximation -- www.thorlabs.com/thorproduct.cfm?partnumber=BS013"
bs_3070_vis_45,,bs_3070_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 30:70) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
bs_7030_vis_45,,bs_7030_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 70:30) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
bs_4060_vis_45,,bs_4060_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 40:60) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
bs_6040_vis_45,,bs_6040_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 60:40) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
bs_9010_vis_45,,bs_9010_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 90:10) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
bs_1090_vis_45,,bs_1090_vis_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: scaled from bs_5050_vis_45 (ratio 10:90) -- each wavelength row keeps Rs+Ts == Rp+Tp == the source row's total (R+T), and the source's s/p asymmetry style (Rs-Rp == -(Ts-Tp)) scaled by 4*rR*rT so it stays in [0,1] at extreme ratios; illustrative, not a vendor part"
pellicle_4555_45,,pellicle_4555_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: modeled on a coated pellicle beamsplitter (e.g. Thorlabs/Edmund 45deg pellicle BS lines): thin (~2 micron) nitrocellulose/UV-cure polymer membrane, negligible dispersion over the visible, flat R:T=45:55 with ~1% total absorption (typical for a coated pellicle); illustrative flat approximation, not a digitized vendor curve"
pellicle_uncoated_45,,pellicle_uncoated_45.mietab,45,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: modeled on an UNCOATED pellicle membrane at 45deg AOI: flat R~8%:T~92% (single thin-film Fresnel reflectance of the bare polymer membrane, no dielectric enhancement coating) with ~1% total absorption; illustrative flat approximation, not a digitized vendor curve"
nd_refl_od03,,nd_refl_od03.mietab,0,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: illustrative Inconel-style metallic neutral-density reflector, flat 400-1100nm at 0deg AOI, OD0.3 (T=10^-OD=0.501187); metallic absorption modeled as A=0.25*(1-T) (approximates the typical partial-absorption fraction of a thin absorbing-metal ND mirror coating, e.g. Inconel/chromium), R=1-T-A, Rs=Rp and Ts=Tp (non-polarizing at normal incidence); not a digitized vendor curve"
nd_refl_od06,,nd_refl_od06.mietab,0,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: illustrative Inconel-style metallic neutral-density reflector, flat 400-1100nm at 0deg AOI, OD0.6 (T=10^-OD=0.251189); metallic absorption modeled as A=0.25*(1-T) (approximates the typical partial-absorption fraction of a thin absorbing-metal ND mirror coating, e.g. Inconel/chromium), R=1-T-A, Rs=Rp and Ts=Tp (non-polarizing at normal incidence); not a digitized vendor curve"
nd_refl_od10,,nd_refl_od10.mietab,0,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: illustrative Inconel-style metallic neutral-density reflector, flat 400-1100nm at 0deg AOI, OD1.0 (T=10^-OD=0.1); metallic absorption modeled as A=0.25*(1-T) (approximates the typical partial-absorption fraction of a thin absorbing-metal ND mirror coating, e.g. Inconel/chromium), R=1-T-A, Rs=Rp and Ts=Tp (non-polarizing at normal incidence); not a digitized vendor curve"
nd_refl_od20,,nd_refl_od20.mietab,0,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: illustrative Inconel-style metallic neutral-density reflector, flat 400-1100nm at 0deg AOI, OD2.0 (T=10^-OD=0.01); metallic absorption modeled as A=0.25*(1-T) (approximates the typical partial-absorption fraction of a thin absorbing-metal ND mirror coating, e.g. Inconel/chromium), R=1-T-A, Rs=Rp and Ts=Tp (non-polarizing at normal incidence); not a digitized vendor curve"
nd_refl_od30,,nd_refl_od30.mietab,0,"generated by scripts/tools/gen_registry_rows.py: illustrative Inconel-style metallic neutral-density reflector, flat 400-1100nm at 0deg AOI, OD3.0 (T=10^-OD=0.001); metallic absorption modeled as A=0.25*(1-T) (approximates the typical partial-absorption fraction of a thin absorbing-metal ND mirror coating, e.g. Inconel/chromium), R=1-T-A, Rs=Rp and Ts=Tp (non-polarizing at normal incidence); not a digitized vendor curve"
MgF2_633,mgf2:qw@633,,,"Single-layer QW MgF2 AR at 633nm (HeNe); computed R=1.23% on BK7 (Macleod admittance, self-verified); H.A. Macleod Thin-Film Optical Filters 5th ed."
MgF2_1064,mgf2:qw@1064,,,Single-layer QW MgF2 AR at 1064nm (Nd:YAG); computed R=1.26% on BK7 (self-verified); H.A. Macleod Thin-Film Optical Filters 5th ed.
Vcoat_532,mgf2:qw@532;al2o3_film:qw@532,,,"Quarter-quarter 2-layer AR (outer MgF2 / inner Al2O3_film) on BK7; R=0.081%@532 (self-verified). APPROXIMATES a commercial V-coat (real recipe uses non-QWOT high-index layer, Willey Laser Focus World 13-Oct-2016)"
Vcoat_633,mgf2:qw@633;al2o3_film:qw@633,,,Quarter-quarter 2-layer AR at 633nm; R=0.081% (self-verified); V-coat approximation (Willey LFW 2016)
Vcoat_1064,mgf2:qw@1064;al2o3_film:qw@1064,,,Quarter-quarter 2-layer AR at 1064nm; R=0.066% (self-verified); V-coat approximation (Willey LFW 2016)
BBAR_QHQ_550,mgf2:qw@550;ta2o5:qw@550;ta2o5:qw@550;al2o3_film:qw@550,,,"3-layer QHQ/W-coat broadband AR: MgF2(L)/Ta2O5(half-wave H)/Al2O3_film(M) outer-to-substrate, lam0=550; recipe per Willey Laser Focus World 13-Oct-2016 + Notch Optics; 4-layer TMM not hand-verified"
HR_TiO2SiO2_532,tio2:qw@532;sio2_film:qw@532;tio2:qw@532;sio2_film:qw@532;tio2:qw@532;sio2_film:qw@532;tio2:qw@532;sio2_film:qw@532;tio2:qw@532;sio2_film:qw@532;tio2:qw@532,,,"11-layer H(LH)^5 QW HR stack, TiO2/SiO2 on BK7, lam0=532; R=99.97% (Macleod symmetric-period admittance, self-derived); TiO2 index DeVore 1951"
HR_TiO2SiO2_633,tio2:qw@633;sio2_film:qw@633;tio2:qw@633;sio2_film:qw@633;tio2:qw@633;sio2_film:qw@633;tio2:qw@633;sio2_film:qw@633;tio2:qw@633;sio2_film:qw@633;tio2:qw@633,,,11-layer H(LH)^5 QW HR at 633nm; R=99.95% (self-derived); TiO2 DeVore 1951
HR_TiO2SiO2_1064,tio2:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;tio2:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;tio2:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;tio2:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;tio2:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;tio2:qw@1064,,,11-layer H(LH)^5 QW HR at 1064nm; R=99.93% (self-derived); NOTE Ta2O5/SiO2 is the more common low-absorption NIR choice (see HR_Ta2O5SiO2_1064); TiO2 at nk-table edge
HR_Ta2O5SiO2_1064,ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064;sio2_film:qw@1064;ta2o5:qw@1064,,,"15-layer H(LH)^7 QW HR, Ta2O5/SiO2 on BK7, lam0=1064 (more periods due to lower index contrast); R=99.96% (self-derived); conventional 1064nm laser-HR material pair"
protected_aluminum_0,,protected_aluminum_0.mietab,0,"Thorlabs Protected Aluminum (SiO2-protected Al, PF-G01 series): Ravg>90% 450nm-2um; curve shape (incl 750-850nm dip) engineering-approx anchored to vendor band-avg using aluminum.mienk (Rakic 1995) as guide; NOT a digitized vendor curve; thorlabs.com objectgroup_id=1161"
protected_silver_0,,protected_silver_0.mietab,0,"Thorlabs Protected Silver (SiO2-protected Ag): Ravg>97% 450nm-2um, >95% 2-20um; engineering-approx shape anchored to vendor band-avg (blue dip is real Ag behavior); NOT digitized; thorlabs.com objectgroup_id=903"
protected_gold_0,,protected_gold_0.mietab,0,Thorlabs Protected Gold: Ravg>96% 800nm-20um (not used <800nm); engineering-approx smooth IR rise anchored to vendor band-avg; NOT digitized; thorlabs.com objectgroup_id=744
dichroic_805sp_45,,dichroic_805sp_45.mietab,45,"Thorlabs DMSP805 shortpass dichroic @45deg: cutoff 805nm, Tavg>90% 400-790nm, Ravg>90% 820-1300nm; sigmoid+s/p split engineering-approx (band-avg spec, not digitized); opposite polarity to existing dichroic_567lp_45; thorlabs.com item DMSP805"
laser_mirror_1064_45,,laser_mirror_1064_45.mietab,45,CVI Y1-series Nd:YAG laser-line mirror @45deg: Rs>=99.9% Rp>=99.6% on-band 1047-1064nm; off-band rolloff illustrative (only on-band peak vendor-sourced); cvilaseroptics.com Mirrors PDF
bs_5050_vis_45_ph,,bs_5050_vis_45_ph.mietab,45,"P2 phase-column demonstration: Rs/Rp/Ts/Tp magnitudes UNCHANGED from bs_5050_vis_45 (see that row for their derivation/citation); ars_deg/arp_deg/ats_deg/atp_deg columns are COMPUTED (not invented) offline via scripts/raytracer/thinfilm.tmm_coeffs for a simple lossless 1-layer TMM stack: BK7 (n=1.5168) / dielectric interlayer (n=1.70, d=120nm) / BK7, at 45deg AOI, wavelength-independent indices (illustrative, not vendor-measured) -- this is NOT BS013's actual (proprietary, unpublished) phase spectrum, which needs a real multilayer/metal-dielectric design; it demonstrates the Zemax-TABLE-style phase-column format with physically-derived numbers from a real interference calculation, energy-exact (Rs+Ts=Rp+Tp=1 for the TMM design, verified by test_coating_phase.py)"
